## Findings

#### 1. Triple Regex Replace Chain + `.ToLower()` in `Underscore` (1 instance)
🔴 **Critical** — hot path, called millions of times
**Impact:** 4 intermediate string allocations per call (3 regex replaces + 1 ToLower). `Kebaberize` compounds this by adding a 5th allocation via `Dasherize`.
**Files:** `CaseTransformExtensions.cs:L115-121`
**Fix:** Replace the 3-regex chain with a single-pass `StringBuilder` or `string.Create` approach that inserts underscores and lowercases in one traversal.
```csharp
public static string Underscore(this string input)
{
    if (string.IsNullOrEmpty(input)) return input;
    var sb = new StringBuilder(input.Length + 4);
    for (int i = 0; i < input.Length; i++)
    {
        char c = input[i];
        if (char.IsUpper(c))
        {
            if (i > 0)
            {
                char prev = input[i - 1];
                // Insert _ between lowercase/digit and uppercase
                if (char.IsLower(prev) || char.IsDigit(prev))
                    sb.Append('_');
                // Insert _ between uppercase run and uppercase+lowercase (e.g., HTMLParser → html_parser)
                else if (char.IsUpper(prev) && i + 1 < input.Length && char.IsLower(input[i + 1]))
                    sb.Append('_');
            }
            sb.Append(char.ToLowerInvariant(c));
        }
        else if (c == '-' || c == ' ')
